  "review": {
    "review": "The recorded death was caused by a bone explosion: decision 3628 attacked the adjacent wounded summon at 7 HP, and accepted transition 10547 reduced HP to zero. An earlier, actionable defect appears at decision 3614 (selection 10498): after defeating the doorway summon, the bot saw its surviving necromancer and held one usable staff charge, but doorway preparation preempted an admitted stationary shot with a wait. Decisions 3614–3618 advanced time while the caster approached and replaced its minion; subsequent retreat lost more health. The selecting chain is tools/policy_tree.py:26, tools/mage_policy.py:1180 and tools/doorway_tactics.py:129–164 in the played source. A reduced public-input fixture with explicitly supplied hold bookkeeping reproduces the preceding doorway attack and the erroneous wait; this is not a complete runtime reconstruction. The proposed correction intercepts a lone visible summoner from an otherwise valid hold using existing magic/thrown admission, without moving or breaking invisibility. Original-source regression: seven tests, two expected assertion failures. Candidate: seven passing tests; full suite: 1,926 tests passed with four skipped. This establishes selection behavior, not a guaranteed kill or survival. Unknown potions and post-death equipment revelations were not used.",
    "learnings": "A doorway controls approaching melee enemies, not a summoner’s ability to replace them. When the minion is gone, use an already admitted stationary ranged attack on the visible caster rather than granting free lure turns. Keep the established bank, protection, resource and targeting checks; do not assume the shot kills or the room is cleared."
  },
